second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Where is the Kate Chopin House located?\", \"slot_hint\": \"place\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin House (Cloutierville, Louisiana) The Kate Chopin House, also known as the Bayou Folk Museum or Alexic Cloutier House, was a house in Cloutierville, Louisiana.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 171, \"end\": 249, \"text\": \"It was the home of Kate Chopin, author of \\\"The Awakening\\\", after her marriage.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 250, \"end\": 361, \"text\": \"The house was located on Main Street (Louisiana Highway 1) in Cloutierville, in Natchitoches Parish, Louisiana.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 362, \"end\": 517, \"text\": \"The home was built by the town's founder, Alexis Cloutier and was constructed in a combination of handmade brick, hand-hewn cypress boards, and bousillage.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 518, \"end\": 604, \"text\": \"Its construction, done through the use of slave labor, dated to between 1806 and 1813.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"start\": 605, \"end\": 632, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin moved here with\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 166, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin House (New Orleans, Louisiana) The Kate Chopin House, also known as the Bayou Folk Museum or Alexic Cloutier House, was a house in New Orleans, Louisiana.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 167, \"end\": 245, \"text\": \"It was the home of Kate Chopin, author of \\\"The Awakening\\\", after her marriage.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 246, \"end\": 350, \"text\": \"The house was located on Main Street (Louisiana Highway 1) in New Orleans, in Orleans Parish, Louisiana.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 351, \"end\": 506, \"text\": \"The home was built by the town's founder, Alexis Cloutier and was constructed in a combination of handmade brick, hand-hewn cypress boards, and bousillage.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 507, \"end\": 593, \"text\": \"Its construction, done through the use of slave labor, dated to between 1806 and 1813.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d01\", \"start\": 594, \"end\": 690, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin moved here with her husband, Oscar Chopin, in 1879, and they lived there until 1884.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 13, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 14, \"end\": 39, \"text\": \"New York : Ungar , 1986 .\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 40, \"end\": 59, \"text\": \"Koloski , Bernard .\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 60, \"end\": 104, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin : A Study of the Short Fiction .\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 105, \"end\": 131, \"text\": \"New York : Twayne , 1996 .\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 132, \"end\": 136, \"text\": \"Ed .\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 137, \"end\": 188, \"text\": \"Awakenings : The Story of the Kate Chopin Revival .\"}, \"D3S8\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 189, \"end\": 230, \"text\": \"Louisiana State University Press , 2009 .\"}, \"D3S9\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 231, \"end\": 245, \"text\": \"Toth , Emily .\"}, \"D3S10\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 246, \"end\": 259, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin .\"}, \"D3S11\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 260, \"end\": 287, \"text\": \"New York : William Morrow .\"}, \"D3S12\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 288, \"end\": 311, \"text\": \"Unveiling Kate Chopin .\"}, \"D3S13\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 312, \"end\": 362, \"text\": \"Jackson : University Press of Mississippi , 1999 .\"}, \"D3S14\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 363, \"end\": 388, \"text\": \"Per Seyersted , editors .\"}, \"D3S15\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 389, \"end\": 421, \"text\": \"Kate Chopin ’ s Private Papers .\"}, \"D3S16\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 422, \"end\": 469, \"text\": \"Bloomington : Indiana University Press , 1998 .\"}, \"D3S17\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d02\", \"start\": 470, \"end\": 489, \"text\": \"Major Works of Kate\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0022-fdba32f126e9:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Kate Chopin House\